WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:16.362
Bello: Okay. We made it to the filing cabinet.

2
00:00:16.363 --> 00:00:17.694
Dave: Now what?

3
00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:19.732
Brad: We get the nano-putty out.

4
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:24.108
It looks like the drawer is open.

5
00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:26.741
Chuck: But we can't reach the top of the drawer.

6
00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:28.828
It's too high.

7
00:00:28.829 --> 00:00:30.852
Brad: I see that.

8
00:00:30.853 --> 00:00:33.767
Chuck: Well, what do you suggest?

9
00:00:33.768 --> 00:00:35.821
Danny: We need to use─

10
00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:39.647
Dave: ─our imaginations. Yeah, I know.

11
00:00:39.648 --> 00:00:43.800
Give me a hand.

12
00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:48.755
Dave: If we all lift this up, Brad will be able to climb up into the drawer.

13
00:00:48.756 --> 00:00:52.061
Bello: That's a great idea.

14
00:00:52.062 --> 00:01:00.975
Brad: Okay, everybody lift together.

15
00:01:00.976 --> 00:01:06.582
Tina: That was tough!

16
00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:11.807
Chuck: Okay, Brad. Up you go.

17
00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:14.053
Danny: Brad, let me do this.

18
00:01:14.054 --> 00:01:18.008
Danny: I caused all this trouble, I want to help make things right.

19
00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:22.016
Brad: Sure. Do you remember what the nano-putty looks like?

20
00:01:22.017 --> 00:01:25.081
Danny: I can't forget.

21
00:01:25.082 --> 00:01:31.936
Danny: Two centimeters, three centimeters . . . [n3@five centimeters, six centimeters.

22
00:01:31.937 --> 00:01:35.092
Danny: Boy, this is a long ruler.

23
00:01:35.093 --> 00:01:38.592
Fifteen centimeters, sixteen centimeters.

24
00:01:38.593 --> 00:01:40.153
Bello: Keep going, Danny.

25
00:01:40.154 --> 00:01:42.662
You can make it.

26
00:01:42.663 --> 00:01:48.914
Danny: Twenty-six, twenty-seven . . . thirty centimeters.

27
00:01:48.915 --> 00:01:50.255
Danny: I made it!

28
00:01:50.256 --> 00:01:52.529
Wish me luck!

29
00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:56.935
All: Good luck!

30
00:01:56.936 --> 00:02:04.413
Mrs. Rice: Hello? Hello? Is anybody home?

31
00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:06.673
Mrs. Rice: I guess nobody is home.

32
00:02:06.674 --> 00:02:09.309
I should leave a note to warn them.

33
00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:13.125
Mrs. Rice: Now, where is my pen?

34
00:02:13.126 --> 00:02:15.980
What should I write?

35
00:02:15.981 --> 00:02:18.533
Mrs. Rice: "Be very careful.

36
00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:22.216
A dangerous giant might be nearby."

37
00:02:22.217 --> 00:02:37.157
Mrs. Rice: No, no. "A dangerous, invisible giant might be nearby."

38
00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:38.541
Danny: There it is.

39
00:02:38.542 --> 00:02:42.740
I just need to grab a small piece.

40
00:02:42.741 --> 00:02:45.459
Danny: Boy, this is tough stuff.

41
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:51.525
I didn't realize it was so sticky.

42
00:02:51.526 --> 00:02:58.124
Danny: Ugh, this stuff smells when it's up close.

43
00:02:58.125 --> 00:03:04.444
Danny: Now I'm all covered with this stuff! Gross.

44
00:03:04.445 --> 00:03:14.034
Danny: Well, at least I got what I came for.

45
00:03:14.035 --> 00:03:16.536
Danny: Now it's time to get out of here.

46
00:03:16.537 --> 00:03:20.174
Danny: How am I going to climb all the way up there?

47
00:03:20.175 --> 00:03:25.459
Danny: There must be something in this drawer that I can use.

48
00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:29.585
Danny: Ugh, this stuff just sticks to everything.

49
00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:34.422
Danny: It's almost as sticky as chewing gum.

50
00:03:34.423 --> 00:03:36.343
Danny: Hey, wait a minute!

51
00:03:36.344 --> 00:03:39.227
It is as sticky as chewing gum!

52
00:03:39.228 --> 00:03:41.536
Danny: That gives me an idea.

53
00:03:41.537 --> 00:03:44.833
Now, let's hope this works.

54
00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:47.820
Danny: Just as I thought, it sticks.

55
00:03:47.821 --> 00:03:51.252
Brad's not the only one with clever ideas.

56
00:03:51.253 --> 00:03:55.730
Danny: I'm getting good at this kind of climbing.

57
00:03:55.731 --> 00:03:58.889
Danny: I did it!

58
00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.547
Tina: Did you get it?

59
00:04:00.548 --> 00:04:02.158
Danny: I sure did.

60
00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:04.956
I'm coming down now.

61
00:04:04.957 --> 00:04:07.822
Dave: You've got it stuck all over your clothes.

62
00:04:07.823 --> 00:04:11.800
Bello: What happened?

63
00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:14.884
Danny: Yeah, I got it stuck all over me.

64
00:04:14.885 --> 00:04:17.830
Danny: It's a lot messier when you're this small.

65
00:04:17.831 --> 00:04:22.007
Brad: Great. We don't need a lot because the shrink-gun is so small now.

66
00:04:22.008 --> 00:04:31.118
Bello: Okay. Now that we have the nano-putty─

67
00:04:31.119 --> 00:04:33.790
Chuck: It's a giant mouse!

68
00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:39.230
Tina: It's coming straight for us!
